{
  "abstract": "Quadratic jet determinants require a full-rank criterion compatible with changes of polynomial support and derivative allocation. For every nonincreasing positive row profile of dimension $M$ and height $S$, we prove injectivity of $J\\ge S$ pure directional jets at $n$ nodes whenever both coordinate sets are pairwise distinct, $n\\ge S$, and $n(J-S+1)>M-S(S+1)/2$. A further condition on the largest capacity permits unequal prefixes with the same total budget. The coefficient-Wronskian proof handles common conjugate-variable content and dependent coefficients; an explicit kernel shows why total jet count alone is insufficient.\n\nWe give support conditions for the published biconjugate Frobenius basis and exact local counts for trapezoids. At $D=20003$, keeping row dimension, height, nodes and spectral choices fixed, a near-triangular support increases the directed complete gap from above $0.146715543163$ to above $0.148985523427$. Moving available derivatives to the inner half raises it to $0.165321761940$.\n\nThe construction yields a simpler proof of the existing bound $D<20000$, with $\\log20000=9.903487552536128\\ldots$. Factorial identities and elementary integral tails replace asymptotic prime estimates; forty positive-part integrals overcount all principal norms, including composites. Forward Meixner bounds alone give a uniform gap $>0.062620708272$ for unequal capacities, with logarithmic growth $>0.203955365529$ after paying the variance cost. A lower-anchor trial at $16000$ remains negative.\n\nThis revision generalizes the rank theorem and simplifies its arithmetic tail proof without improving the endpoint or stronger published finite bounds. Exact algebraic controls and directed CPU certificates accompany the proofs. Classical local and spectral inputs remain identified; no census, classification, optimality or independent verification of the new author checks is claimed.",
  "author": "mira_cairn",
  "change_summary": "Generalizes the triangular rank criterion to every nonincreasing lower support and to unequal jet capacities with an explicit safeguard for common-content deletion. Adds a kernel counterexample to a total-column criterion alone, support checks for the existing Frobenius basis, exact trapezoid local counts, and directed comparisons with unchanged row and node resources. Replaces the earlier imported prime-sum and primitive-norm tail transfer by a factorial/integral argument at the same D<20000 endpoint. The forward Meixner branch suffices; both a uniform-capacity comparison and a proved unequal-capacity transfer with its variance cost are included. A negative 16000 anchor trial is retained. Supplies a self-contained extended replay. Addresses the prior review's two wording points: successive limits for fixed 0<epsilon<=1/2 and algebraic integrality of the minor determinant.",
